051083 #edb/ref 1031 "LU Factorization of 3x3 Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1033 1780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7fcb6c0b-c77e-5abe-8b04-125d08ffe36e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117301 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eb09a7a1-1cf1-5147-b432-0481d5365f80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117302 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117302 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117302 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "82aab95b-303c-53e6-8ab2-84f6327c5ee5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117303 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117303 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117303 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bcb99789-0a50-51fa-bdd2-8edcdb147b3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117304 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117304 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117304 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c1646219-17da-5382-a70c-29be623f2a43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117305 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117305 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117305 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6fa6c065-8e80-5891-9d48-f1f2b1d88af2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117306 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117306 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117306 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7d799ac4-cfd7-50f4-84fe-96c72faba44f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119605 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119605 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that\n![](images/d4/d4fa85cab74f4bda57059d1c6abc9dacea665531ce84ba9d2f1598a13c49ef60.png) \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119605 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7324b66-d8f7-5bdb-9786-4160808f2a7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119605 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since $E_1A=U,$ we can invert $E_1$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119606 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4769" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119606 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that a $3 \\times 3$ matrix $F$ is reduced to row echelon form using the following elementary row operations, applied in the order in which they appear:\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+R_1, \\qquad\n\tR_3:=R_3+2R_1\n$$\n\nGiven that $F$ has the LU factorization $F=LU,$ then $L=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119606 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58955d86-8a94-5174-83fa-072314037298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119606 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying $R_2:=R_2 + {\\color{red}1} \\cdot R_1$ and then $R_3:=R_3+ {\\color{red}2} \\cdot R_1$ is equivalent to multiplying $F$ from the left by the following elementary matrices:\n\n![](images/5e/5eb696ca679a0079e8460d472b6f172df4f2e29f5dfef6cbdee388c55dcb1db5.png)\n\nNow, since $E_2E_1F=U,$ we can invert $E_2$ and $E_1$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}F & =U \\\\ {E}_{1}F & ={E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ F & ={E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ F & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ F & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])U \\\\ F & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot U\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119607 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4770" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119607 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that\n![](images/e8/e85dac75798b6cb463403f54ab2a675206d7eeea0a8958081aac9c696047b345.png)\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119607 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50685ac4-9980-5841-a669-783f6086a9dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119607 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 11 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{5}{4}){R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{2}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot {E}_{1}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since $E_2E_1A=U,$ we can invert $E_2$ and $E_1$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ {E}_{1}A & ={E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}])U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119794 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119794 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186243964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302221 #edb/ref 1759218604541